Create an IAM role as below:

1) IAM role name must be iamrole_javed.

aws-client ~ ➜  touch iamrole_javed.json

aws-client ~ ➜  vi iamrole_javed.json 

aws-client ~ ➜  aws iam create-role --role-name iamrole_javed --assume-role-policy-document file://iamrole_javed.json
{
    "Role": {
        "Path": "/",
        "RoleName": "iamrole_javed",
        "RoleId": "AROAWVGJRPBYCCDCXQIP5",
        "Arn": "arn:aws:iam::457836689520:role/iamrole_javed",
        "CreateDate": "2026-04-29T01:27:09Z",
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": {
            "Version": "2012-10-17",
            "Statement": [
                {
                    "Effect": "Allow",
                    "Principal": {
                        "Service": "ec2.amazonaws.com"
                    },
                    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
                }
            ]
        }
    }
}

2) Entity type must be AWS Service and use case must be EC2.
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": { "Service": "ec2.amazonaws.com" },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}




3) Attach a policy named iampolicy_javed.
aws-client ~ ➜  aws iam list-policies --query "Policies[?PolicyName=='iampolicy_javed'].Arn" --output text
arn:aws:iam::457836689520:policy/iampolicy_javed

aws-client ~ ➜  aws iam attach-role-policy --role-name iamrole_javed --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::457836689520:policy/iampolicy_javed

aws-client ~ ➜  aws iam list-attached-role-policies --role-name iamrole_javed
{
    "AttachedPolicies": [
        {
            "PolicyName": "iampolicy_javed",
            "PolicyArn": "arn:aws:iam::457836689520:policy/iampolicy_javed"
        }
    ]
}


